---
export const prerender = true

import '../styles/global.css'
import InfoCard from '../components/InfoCard.astro'
import GenericPageWrapper from '../components/GenericPageWrapper.astro'
---

<style>
	.InfoCardHolder {
		width:100%;
		display:flex;
		flex-direction:column;
		align-items:center;
		justify-content:center;
	}
</style>

<GenericPageWrapper>
	<div role="main" class="InfoCardHolder">
	<div style="width:80%;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:10px;">
	<InfoCard title="Introduction" content="Hello! I am Maia, and I'm studying Computer Science BSc.
	I have an avid interest in software, trains and the Meshtastic project, just to name a few.
	The personal projects I am currently working on include a 
	<a href='https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/data/instruments/srtm'>SRTM</a> dataset plotter, a bridge
	between my meshtastic node and this website, and a game where the player must connect various 
	industries by designing their own railway
	system.
	<br/><br/>
	My favourite language is Rust (and my favourite engine is Bevy) though I also have experience with Java, Javascript, Lua and Python."/>
	
	<InfoCard title="This website" content="I made this website with Astro and deployed it on cloudflare workers. It serves the purpose of
	being my personal portfolio as well as a place to experiment with web technology and to show off my hobbies. PS:
	my logo design is inspired from Southeastern railway's logo, because they operate my favourite train class."/>

	<InfoCard title="Things I think are worth checking out" content="Consider taking a look at the 
	<a href='https://meshtastic.org/docs/getting-started/'>Meshtastic project</a>,
	I personally operate 2 nodes (A Heltec V3 at home, and a T1000-E for carrying around). 
	It's a fun hobby, and a great way to meet other people!"/>

	</div>
	</div>
</GenericPageWrapper>